```python
from fractions import Fraction

def step(mu, P):
    k = len(P)
    return [sum(mu[i] * P[i][j] for i in range(k)) for j in range(k)]

def power_iterate(mu, P, n):
    for _ in range(n):
        mu = step(mu, P)
    return mu

def is_stationary(pi, P):
    return step(pi, P) == pi
```

From the closed form of $P^n$, $(P^n)_{11} = \frac{b + a\lambda^n}{a + b}$ with $\lambda = 1 - a - b = \tfrac14$, so $(P^n)_{11} - \pi_1 = \frac{a}{a + b}\lambda^n = \frac13 \cdot 4^{-n}$ exactly — which the test checks in rational arithmetic.
